{
  "slug": "artist:gucci-mane",
  "name": "Gucci Mane",
  "editorial_article": "Born Radric Delantic Davis in Bessemer, Alabama, the Atlanta-based rapper rose to prominence by pioneering the trap music genre for mainstream audiences during the 2000s. His independent 2005 debut album Trap House, released via Big Cat Records, reached the Billboard Heatseekers chart and established his influence in the Southern hip-hop scene. He achieved his first chart-topping success as a featured artist on the 2016 Rae Sremmurd single Black Beatles, which held the number one spot on the Billboard Hot 100 for seven non-consecutive weeks. Through his 1017 Records imprint, founded in 2007, he has fostered the careers of artists such as Young Thug, Waka Flocka Flame, and Chief Keef. Known for a prolific recording pace, his career has spanned over 16 studio albums and 71 mixtapes, often produced by longtime collaborator Zaytoven, with whom he crafted his seminal underground sound.",
